msgid "[b]Datos[/b]\n• Fronteras políticas: [url=https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria]Cliopatria[/url], Seshat Global History Databank, CC BY 4.0.\n• Costas, lagos, ríos y países actuales: [url=https://www.naturalearthdata.com]Natural Earth[/url], dominio público.\n• Población por país: [url=https://ourworldindata.org/population-sources]Our World in Data[/url] (HYDE 3.3, Gapminder y ONU, World Population Prospects 2024), CC BY 4.0.\n• Relieve: GEBCO 2008 en la versión de la NASA; color del terreno: NASA Blue Marble Next Generation (julio de 2004), dominio público.\n• Textos de la enciclopedia: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0) y los paquetes propios en data/enciclopedia.\n• Lugares antiguos: [url=https://pleiades.stoa.org]Pleiades[/url] (ISAW, Universidad de Nueva York, y Ancient World Mapping Center), CC BY 3.0.\n[b]Tipografías[/b]\n• Cinzel y EB Garamond, SIL Open Font License."
msgstr "[b]Data[/b]\n• Political borders: [url=https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria]Cliopatria[/url], Seshat Global History Databank, CC BY 4.0.\n• Coastlines, lakes, rivers and present-day countries: [url=https://www.naturalearthdata.com]Natural Earth[/url], public domain.\n• Population by country: [url=https://ourworldindata.org/population-sources]Our World in Data[/url] (HYDE 3.3, Gapminder and the UN's World Population Prospects 2024), CC BY 4.0.\n• Relief: GEBCO 2008 in NASA's version; terrain color: NASA Blue Marble Next Generation (July 2004), public domain.\n• Encyclopedia texts: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0) and TellMAP's own packages in data/enciclopedia.\n• Ancient places: [url=https://pleiades.stoa.org]Pleiades[/url] (ISAW, New York University, and the Ancient World Mapping Center), CC BY 3.0.\n[b]Typefaces[/b]\n• Cinzel and EB Garamond, SIL Open Font License."

